<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ludwig of Oettingen-Wallerstein</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1791–1870</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prince Ludwig of Oettingen-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wallerstein">Wallerstein</a> was a Bavarian statesman who served King Ludwig I as interior minister from 1832 to 1837 and led the government again in 1847–1848, during the crisis over the king's affair with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lola-montez">Lola Montez</a>. He had given up the headship of his house to his brother after an unequal marriage in 1823.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ludwig-of-oettingen-wallerstein.jpg" alt="Ludwig of Oettingen-Wallerstein" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LodewijkOettingen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
